  "title": "nstime: Don't overflow in nstime_cmp",
  "description": "nstime_cmp can overflow unnecessarily and give the opposite result\nin cases where a time_t is bigger than an int (e.g., 64-bit and 32-bit,\nas on many platforms) and two times differ by more than INT_MAX.\n\nJust return -1, 0, and 1. If it's truly useful to return something like\n\"the difference in the time in seconds, rounded away from zero,\" we\ncould do that with C23 checked integer arithmetic. (However, the old\nimplemention couldn't be counted on to do that, and it would return\nthe difference in the nanoseconds if the seconds were equal.)\n\nFix #16463",
